IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gst-registration`

-- A New Tax System (Goods and Services Tax) Act 1999 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- GST amounts the registration baseline
-- could not compute, now computed from the formulas the Federal Register prints as images: the value of a supply that is only
-- partly taxable, from its taxable proportion (s 9-80); the adjustments for a change in the extent of creditable purpose
-- (Division 129: ss 129-20, 129-40, 129-70, 129-75); and the adjustment on cancelling registration (s 138-5).
--
-- A module beside gst-registration.l4 (24 October 2026). gst-registration.l4 asks for the GST-free or input taxed part of a
-- supply's price in dollars, and lists Divisions 19 and 21 and the other adjustments as not encoded. It stays as it is; this
-- module calls its `What is the value of a taxable supply` (s 9-75) rather than restating it.
--
-- SEAT: the individual who carries on an enterprise (a sole trader such as Jake, if he registers): "How much GST is on a sale
-- that is partly GST-free?", "I used my van less for the business than I expected -- what must I pay back?", "I am cancelling my
-- registration -- what do I owe on what I still hold?"
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 96 (register id C2026C00081), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00446.txt. The formulas are
-- transcribed in ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00446.formulas.md (entries s 9-80(2), s 129-70, s 129-75, s 138-5(2);
-- recovered 2026-10-24), and encoded from there.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. How the taxable proportion and the extents of application are measured (the person states them, as
-- percentages or a proportion); s 129-25 (disposal, loss or end of a limited period shortening the adjustment periods); the
-- Commissioner's determination of fewer adjustment periods (s 129-20(3), last sentence); whether an acquisition "relates to
-- business finance" (asked as a fact); Division 129's other rules (ss 129-45, 129-50, 129-55 and the reduced credit rule of
-- s 129-40(3)); s 129-80 (earlier adjustments, which the person takes into account in the full input tax credit); importations
-- (s 138-5(2)(c)); s 138-17 (deceased estates); Division 162 (GST instalments) and the other Chapter 4 formulas.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual to whom the law is applied,
-- with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate.
-- Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `A New Tax System (Goods and Services Tax) Act 1999 -- amounts from the formulas`

§§ `s 9-80 -- a supply that is partly GST-free or input taxed`

-- s 9-80(1): "the value of the part of the actual supply that is a taxable supply is the proportion of the value of the actual
-- supply that the taxable supply represents." (2), from the authorised rendering:
--     (*Price of the actual supply × 10) / (10 + Taxable proportion)
-- "taxable proportion is the proportion of the value of the actual supply that represents the value of the *taxable supply
-- (expressed as a number between 0 and 1)." With s 9-70, the GST is 10% of the taxable part's value.
@export What is the value of my supply that is partly GST-free or input taxed, in dollars (s 9-80(2))?
GIVEN `price of the whole supply` IS A NUMBER @desc The price of the whole supply, in dollars, including any GST
      `taxable proportion` IS A NUMBER @desc The proportion of the supply's value that is the taxable part, as a number between 0 and 1
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the value of my partly taxable supply` MEANS
    (`price of the whole supply` TIMES 10) DIVIDED BY (10 PLUS `taxable proportion`)

@export How much GST is on my supply that is partly GST-free or input taxed, in dollars (ss 9-70, 9-80)?
GIVEN `price of the whole supply` IS A NUMBER @desc The price of the whole supply, in dollars, including any GST
      `taxable proportion` IS A NUMBER @desc The proportion of the supply's value that is the taxable part, as a number between 0 and 1
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much GST is on my partly taxable supply` MEANS
    (`What is the value of my partly taxable supply` `price of the whole supply` `taxable proportion` TIMES `taxable proportion` TIMES 10) DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `Division 129 -- when I use a thing more or less for my enterprise than I claimed`

-- s 129-20(1): an adjustment period is a tax period that "starts at least 12 months after the end of the tax period to which the
-- acquisition ... is attributable" and ends on 30 June (or closest to it). (2), an acquisition that relates to business finance:
-- "(a) ... $50,000 or less -- only the first such tax period"; "(b) more than $50,000 but less than $500,000 -- only the first 5";
-- "(c) $500,000 or more -- only the first 10". (3), one that does not: "(a) ... $5,000 or less -- only the first 2"; "(b) more
-- than $5,000 but less than $500,000 -- only the first 5"; "(c) $500,000 or more -- only the first 10".
@export How many adjustment periods does my acquisition have (s 129-20(2), (3))?
GIVEN `GST exclusive value of the acquisition` IS A NUMBER @desc What the thing cost you, leaving out the GST, in dollars
      `it relates to business finance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the acquisition relates to business finance (borrowing or lending as a business)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many adjustment periods do I have` MEANS
    IF `it relates to business finance`
    THEN (IF `GST exclusive value of the acquisition` AT MOST 50000 THEN 1
          ELSE IF `GST exclusive value of the acquisition` LESS THAN 500000 THEN 5 ELSE 10)
    ELSE (IF `GST exclusive value of the acquisition` AT MOST 5000 THEN 2
          ELSE IF `GST exclusive value of the acquisition` LESS THAN 500000 THEN 5 ELSE 10)

-- s 129-40(1) Steps 1 to 5: the actual application (the extent applied for a creditable purpose from acquisition to the end of the
-- adjustment period) against the intended or former application (the extent intended on acquisition, or the actual application
-- at the last adjustment); less is an increasing adjustment, more a decreasing one, the same neither. (2): as percentages.
-- s 129-70, from the authorised rendering:
--     Increasing adjustment = Full input tax credit × (*Intended or former application − *Actual application)
-- s 129-75:   Decreasing adjustment = Full input tax credit × (*Actual application − *Intended or former application)
-- "full input tax credit is the amount of the input tax credit to which you would have been entitled ... if: (a) the acquisition
-- ... had been solely for a *creditable purpose". For a taxable supply to you at its full price, that is the GST in the price:
-- s 9-75's value x 10% (gst-registration.l4).
DECLARE `Division 129 adjustment` IS ONE OF
    `an increasing adjustment` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `a decreasing adjustment` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no adjustment: the actual application is the same as the intended or former application`
    `no adjustment: this tax period is not one of the acquisition's adjustment periods`

@export What adjustment do I have for this adjustment period, for using a thing more or less for my enterprise than I claimed (ss 129-20, 129-40, 129-70, 129-75)?
GIVEN `price I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc What you paid for the thing, in dollars, including GST (the supply to you being taxable at its full price)
      `it relates to business finance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the acquisition relates to business finance
      `which adjustment period this is` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for the first tax period ending on 30 June that starts at least 12 months after the period you claimed the credit in, 2 for the next, and so on
      `intended or former application in percent` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage you acquired it for a creditable purpose (or, if you have had a Division 129 adjustment for it, the actual application at the last one)
      `actual application in percent` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage you have actually applied it for a creditable purpose from acquisition to the end of this period
GIVETH A `Division 129 adjustment`
`What Division 129 adjustment do I have` MEANS
    IF `which adjustment period this is` LESS THAN 1 OR `which adjustment period this is` GREATER THAN (`How many adjustment periods do I have` (`What is the value of a taxable supply` `price I paid`) `it relates to business finance`)
    THEN `no adjustment: this tax period is not one of the acquisition's adjustment periods`
    ELSE IF `actual application in percent` LESS THAN `intended or former application in percent`
         THEN `an increasing adjustment` ((`the full input tax credit` TIMES (`intended or former application in percent` MINUS `actual application in percent`)) DIVIDED BY 100)
         ELSE IF `actual application in percent` GREATER THAN `intended or former application in percent`
              THEN `a decreasing adjustment` ((`the full input tax credit` TIMES (`actual application in percent` MINUS `intended or former application in percent`)) DIVIDED BY 100)
              ELSE `no adjustment: the actual application is the same as the intended or former application`
    WHERE
        `the full input tax credit` MEANS (`What is the value of a taxable supply` `price I paid` TIMES 10) DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `s 138-5 -- cancelling my registration`

-- s 138-5(1): an increasing adjustment if "(a) your *registration is cancelled; and (b) immediately before the cancellation takes
-- effect, your assets include anything in respect of which you were, or are, entitled to an input tax credit."
-- (2), from the authorised rendering:   (1 / 11) × *Actual application of the thing × Applicable value
-- "applicable value is: (a) the *GST inclusive market value of the thing immediately before the cancellation takes effect; or (b) if
-- you were, or are, entitled to an input tax credit for acquiring the thing -- the amount of the *consideration that you provided,
-- or were liable to provide, for your acquisition of the thing, but only if the amount is less than that value".
-- (3): no adjustment if there were adjustment periods for the acquisition and "the last of those adjustment periods has ended
-- before the cancellation of your *registration takes effect".
DECLARE `Cancellation adjustment` IS ONE OF
    `an increasing adjustment on cancellation` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no adjustment: the last adjustment period for the thing ended before the cancellation (s 138-5(3))`
    `no adjustment: I was never entitled to an input tax credit for the thing`

@export What increasing adjustment do I have for a thing I hold when my GST registration is cancelled (s 138-5)?
GIVEN `I was entitled to an input tax credit for acquiring it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were (or are) entitled to an input tax credit for acquiring the thing
      `its last adjustment period ended before the cancellation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the thing had adjustment periods and the last of them ended before the cancellation takes effect
      `actual application in percent` IS A NUMBER @desc The extent, as a percentage, you have applied the thing for a creditable purpose (its actual application)
      `GST inclusive market value just before the cancellation` IS A NUMBER @desc The thing's market value, including GST, immediately before the cancellation takes effect, in dollars
      `what I paid for it` IS A NUMBER @desc The consideration you provided, or were liable to provide, for acquiring it, in dollars
GIVETH A `Cancellation adjustment`
`What adjustment do I have on cancelling my registration` MEANS
    IF NOT `I was entitled to an input tax credit for acquiring it`
    THEN `no adjustment: I was never entitled to an input tax credit for the thing`
    ELSE IF `its last adjustment period ended before the cancellation`
         THEN `no adjustment: the last adjustment period for the thing ended before the cancellation (s 138-5(3))`
         ELSE `an increasing adjustment on cancellation` ((`actual application in percent` TIMES `the applicable value`) DIVIDED BY (11 TIMES 100))
    WHERE
        `the applicable value` MEANS
            IF `what I paid for it` LESS THAN `GST inclusive market value just before the cancellation`
            THEN `what I paid for it`
            ELSE `GST inclusive market value just before the cancellation`
